    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract thinking and practical problem-solving—something I enjoy when it’s applied to real-world challenges, like optimizing routes for my cycling trips or analyzing data from my photography projects. However, its rigid structure can sometimes feel alienating, especially when dealing with complex equations. It’s both a tool and a puzzle that keeps me engaged.",
